那加了肉汁的土豆泥呢？

367
00:10:13.910 --> 00:10:14.390
Come on.
拜托。

368
00:10:14.550 --> 00:10:15.350
Oh, come on.
哦，拜托。

369
00:10:15.470 --> 00:10:15.590
Yeah.
对。

370
00:10:15.730 --> 00:10:17.990
With the scoop and then the scoop of the gravy.
先盛一勺，然后再浇上一勺肉汁。

371
00:10:18.230 --> 00:10:19.750
Yes, and then you make a little like pond.
对，然后你弄个小水塘一样的形状。

372
00:10:20.370 --> 00:10:24.830
I liked that when I was younger, but something has happened to my potato palate.
我小时候挺喜欢的，但我的土豆品味发生了一些变化。

373
00:10:25.030 --> 00:10:26.990
And I just, it's a pass.
我就是，算了吧。

374
00:10:27.190 --> 00:10:29.930
Do you just equate it with like kind of, it's juvenile?
你是不是觉得它有点像，比较幼稚？

375
00:10:30.510 --> 00:10:31.270
It's like too.
感觉太...

376
00:10:31.350 --> 00:10:32.270
No, it's Thanksgiving.
不，那是感恩节。

377
00:10:32.590 --> 00:10:35.570
Is it too many starches for your all protein weightlifting diet?
是因为你那全是蛋白质的增肌饮食，觉得淀粉太多了吗？

378
00:10:36.230 --> 00:10:36.910
Yes, no.
对，也不是。

379
00:10:37.290 --> 00:10:40.610
It's that I'd rather roast them than have them mashed.
是我宁愿烤着吃也不想吃土豆泥。

380
00:10:40.730 --> 00:10:44.370
In my family, this is the big thing because everybody else likes mashed potatoes.
在我家里，这可是件大事，因为其他人都喜欢土豆泥。

381
00:10:44.370 --> 00:10:49.930
And sometimes I hit a wall and I roast the potatoes and it's a whole thing at dinner.
有时候我实在忍无可忍，就烤了土豆，晚餐时就会闹得沸沸扬扬。

382
00:10:50.390 --> 00:10:52.730
They're like, oh, mom roasted the potatoes tonight.
他们会说，哦，妈妈今晚烤土豆了。

383
00:10:53.110 --> 00:10:54.070
This is so funny.
这太搞笑了。

384
00:10:54.170 --> 00:10:55.350
I have the complete opposite.
我完全相反。

385
00:10:55.610 --> 00:10:58.070
I'm like the one that loves mashed potatoes and my kids don't.
我是那个超爱土豆泥的人，但我孩子们不爱。

386
00:10:58.150 --> 00:10:59.930
And I'm like, how can you not love mashed potatoes?
然后我就想，怎么会有人不爱土豆泥呢？

387
00:11:00.330 --> 00:11:01.410
How is this possible?
这怎么可能？

388
00:11:01.710 --> 00:11:01.970
Hmm.
嗯。

389
00:11:02.290 --> 00:11:04.250
It sounds to me like potato eating.
在我看来，关于吃土豆这事。

390
00:11:04.410 --> 00:11:05.430
We need to switch families.
我们需要交换家庭。

391
00:11:05.610 --> 00:11:05.730
Yeah.
对。

392
00:11:05.990 --> 00:11:06.150
Okay.
好吧。

393
00:11:07.210 --> 00:11:08.410
And then everyone's happy.
这样大家就都开心了。

394
00:11:08.690 --> 00:11:08.850
Yeah.
是啊。

395
00:11:09.050 --> 00:11:09.510
I don't know.
我不知道。

396
00:11:09.650 --> 00:11:09.790
Potato swap.
土豆互换。

397
00:11:09.790 --> 00:11:13.270
Jenna, I'm just really disappointed in you right now.
珍娜，我现在对你真的很失望。

398
00:11:13.390 --> 00:11:13.530
Yeah.
对。

399
00:11:13.850 --> 00:11:13.970
Shoot.
糟了。

400
00:11:14.170 --> 00:11:18.410
I used to bet they'd be at the bottom, but I'd rather have a scalloped.
我以前打赌它们会排在最后，但我宁愿吃烤土豆片。

401
00:11:18.630 --> 00:11:19.490
I'd rather have gnocchi.
我宁愿吃意式面疙瘩。

402
00:11:20.250 --> 00:11:22.190
Last kind of potato I want is mashed.
土豆最不想要的做法就是土豆泥。

403
00:11:22.390 --> 00:11:23.110
I'm sorry I said it.
我很抱歉我这么说了。

404
00:11:23.190 --> 00:11:25.030
Scalloped is at the bottom of my liSt.
烤土豆片在我这里排在最底部。

405
00:11:25.330 --> 00:11:25.650
Really?
真的吗？

406
00:11:25.890 --> 00:11:26.150
Yeah.
对啊。

407
00:11:26.510 --> 00:11:27.810
You know, they're fine.
你知道的，它们其实挺好的。

408
00:11:28.010 --> 00:11:29.170
I like a scalloped potato.
我挺喜欢烤土豆片的。

409
00:11:29.390 --> 00:11:32.130
And also my husband makes a thing called a potato stack.
而且我老公还会做一种叫土豆塔的东西。

410
00:11:32.450 --> 00:11:33.250
So good.
超级好吃。

411
00:11:33.370 --> 00:11:35.930
It's like thinly sliced potatoes and then he bakes some stuff.
就像是切得薄薄的土豆片，然后他会加些料烤一下。

412
00:11:36.010 --> 00:11:36.150
Oh, that's good.
哦，那听起来不错。

413
00:11:36.430 --> 00:11:36.630
Yeah.
对啊。

414
00:11:37.010 --> 00:11:37.970
But I don't know.
不过我不知道。

415
00:11:38.110 --> 00:11:39.510
I'm just always going to go French fry.
我最后肯定还是会选炸薯条。

416
00:11:39.790 --> 00:11:40.010
Yeah.
对啊。

417
00:11:40.130 --> 00:11:40.270
Yeah.
没错。

418
00:11:40.350 --> 00:11:40.550
Same.
一样。

419
00:11:40.890 --> 00:11:40.990
Yeah.
对啊。

420
00:11:41.130 --> 00:11:41.230
Same.
一样。

421
00:11:41.670 --> 00:11:42.050
All right.
好吧。

422
00:11:42.170 --> 00:11:44.210
We didn't know we could talk about this for so long.
我们都不知道这话题居然能聊这么久。

423
00:11:44.470 --> 00:11:44.710
We didn't.
确实没想到。

424
00:11:44.790 --> 00:11:45.250
We didn't.
真的没想到。

425
00:11:45.490 --> 00:11:46.550
You were right.
你说的对。

426
00:11:47.290 --> 00:11:48.750
Well, listen, why don't we take a break?
好了，听着，我们为什么不休息一下呢？

427
00:11:48.890 --> 00:11:53.110
And then when we come back, we will talk with Randall all about the office and other
等我们回来后，我们会和兰德尔好好聊聊关于《办公室》以及其他

428
00:11:53.110 --> 00:11:53.450
things.
事情。

429
00:11:53.670 --> 00:11:53.930
Yes.
好的。

430
00:11:54.110 --> 00:11:54.290
Great.
太棒了。

431
00:12:04.460 --> 00:12:07.160
We have to ask you a few questions about your time on the office.
我们得问你几个关于你在《办公室》里那段经历的问题。

432
00:12:07.340 --> 00:12:09.760
My very brief time on the office.
我在《办公室》里那段非常短暂的经历。

433
00:12:10.060 --> 00:12:10.560
But iconic.
但绝对是标志性的。

434
00:12:10.900 --> 00:12:12.960
First of all, how did you get your role on the office?
首先，你是怎么得到《办公室》里那个角色的？

435
00:12:13.380 --> 00:12:16.300
You know, so I was in the last season.
你知道的，我是在最后一季加入的。

436
00:12:16.540 --> 00:12:16.720
Yes.
对的。

437
00:12:17.660 --> 00:12:19.200
Somewhere towards the end there.
差不多是在尾声的时候。

438
00:12:19.460 --> 00:12:20.240
The last season.
最后一季。

439
00:12:20.480 --> 00:12:25.620
But a few years before that, I auditioned for like a regular role.
但在那之前的几年，我曾去试镜过一个常规角色。

440
00:12:25.780 --> 00:12:29.120
I was very excited because it's the office.
我当时超级兴奋，因为那是《办公室》。

441
00:12:29.720 --> 00:12:33.180
And I got a call and it was like, they really like you.
然后我接到一个电话，大意是他们真的很喜欢我。

442
00:12:33.240 --> 00:12:33.920
They want to meet you.
他们想见见我。

443
00:12:33.920 --> 00:12:41.080
So I went to the studio and I knew Brent Forrester because I had done a pilot of his years before
所以我去了片场，我认识布伦特·福斯特，因为几年前我演过他制作的一个试播集

444
00:12:41.080 --> 00:12:46.800
and he was showing me around and I was just, oh my God, I'm going to be a regular on this
他带着我四处参观，我当时简直，天哪，我要成为这部剧的常规演员了。

445
00:12:46.800 --> 00:12:47.120
show.
剧集。

446
00:12:47.120 --> 00:12:52.360
So I met with all the writers, like in a big room, all the writers met with me and I met
所以我见到了所有的编剧，在一个大房间里，所有的编剧都见了我，我还见到了

447
00:12:52.360 --> 00:12:56.980
with Mindy and Daniel and Paul and it was great.
明迪、丹尼尔和保罗，感觉太棒了。

448
00:12:57.160 --> 00:13:01.940
And then I went home and I was like, I'm going to, I'm going to be a regular on the office.
然后我回到家，心里想，我要，我要成为《办公室》的常规演员了。

449
00:13:02.060 --> 00:13:02.920
This is crazy.
这太疯狂了。

450
00:13:02.920 --> 00:13:04.400
Oh no.
哦，不会吧。

451
00:13:05.000 --> 00:13:32.880
Oh no.
哦，不。

452
00:13:32.880 --> 00:13:34.060
And then a few years later, I just got a call.
然后几年后，我突然接到一个电话。

453
00:13:34.120 --> 00:13:35.380
Hey, do you want to come on and play?
嘿，你想不想来客串一下？

454
00:13:35.920 --> 00:13:37.980
Like, and I was like, yeah, sure.
就那种，我说，行啊，当然。

455
00:13:38.440 --> 00:13:40.840
And I figured, you know, they all knew me at this point.
我想着，你知道的，那时候他们都已经认识我了。

456
00:13:40.880 --> 00:13:42.420
So I didn't audition or anything.
所以我根本没去试镜什么的。

457
00:13:42.540 --> 00:13:44.240
They just were like, come on and do this.
他们直接就说，来吧，把这个演了。

458
00:13:44.340 --> 00:13:46.140
And then it was just for a cold open.
然后那其实只是个开场戏。

459
00:13:46.320 --> 00:13:47.960
It was really funny and it was great.
真的很有趣，而且感觉超棒。

460
00:13:47.960 --> 00:13:49.360
And I was like, great.
我就想，太棒了。

461
00:13:49.460 --> 00:13:53.480
I get to be on the show, even if it's just like a scene.
我能上这个节目了，哪怕只是一场戏。

462
00:13:53.680 --> 00:13:55.480
And then it was kind of a whirlwind.
接着这一切就像旋风一样。

463
00:13:55.640 --> 00:14:00.700
It was all very quick, you know, it was very quick and I was kind of in and out and had a
一切都太快了，你知道的，非常快，我就这么进进出出，而且

464
00:14:00.700 --> 00:14:01.040
blaSt.
玩得超开心。

465
00:14:01.220 --> 00:14:02.220
And then that was it.
然后就结束了。

466
00:14:02.700 --> 00:14:08.140
Well, this cold open has gone on to become a fan favorite.
嗯，这个开场戏后来成了粉丝最爱的片段之一。

467
00:14:08.600 --> 00:14:09.700
It is iconic.
这太经典了。

468
00:14:10.500 --> 00:14:11.380
Should we hear it?
我们要听听看吗？

469
00:14:11.540 --> 00:14:12.020
We should.
应该听听。

470
00:14:12.180 --> 00:14:13.080
It's season nine.
这是第九季。

471
00:14:13.380 --> 00:14:15.180
The episode is Andy's Ancestry.
这一集是《安迪的祖先》。

472
00:14:15.620 --> 00:14:16.440
Here it is.
就是这个。

473
00:14:21.360 --> 00:14:22.020
Morning, Dwight.
早啊，德怀特。

474
00:14:25.030 --> 00:14:26.130
Who are you?
你是谁？

475
00:14:27.310 --> 00:14:28.210
Who am I?
我是谁？

476
00:14:29.110 --> 00:14:29.950
I'm Jim.
我是吉姆。

477
00:14:30.250 --> 00:14:31.930
We've been working together for 12 years.
我们一起工作12年了。

478
00:14:32.790 --> 00:14:33.650
Weird joke, Dwight.
这笑话真冷，德怀特。

479
00:14:34.250 --> 00:14:35.170
You're not Jim.
你不是吉姆。

480
00:14:35.350 --> 00:14:36.170
Jim's not Asian.
吉姆不是亚洲人。

481
00:14:36.770 --> 00:14:37.970
You seriously never noticed?
你真的从来没注意到吗？

482
00:14:38.310 --> 00:14:40.570
Hey, hats off to you for not seeing race.
嘿，真佩服你能够无视种族。

483
00:14:43.800 --> 00:14:44.620
All right then, Jim.
那好吧，吉姆。

484
00:14:45.460 --> 00:14:48.520
Why don't you tell me about that sale that you made yesterday?
你跟我说说你昨天谈成的那个买卖呗？

485
00:14:49.800 --> 00:14:53.740
Wellington Systems sold them 10 cases of 24-pound letter stock.
惠灵顿系统公司，卖给他们10箱24磅的信纸。

486
00:14:53.920 --> 00:14:55.720
Or were you talking about Krieger Murphy?
还是说你指的是克里格·墨菲公司？

487
00:14:55.720 --> 00:14:56.980
Because I didn't close that one yet.
因为那一单我还没敲定。

488
00:14:57.160 --> 00:15:00.280
But I'm hoping I've got a voicemail from Paul Krieger waiting for me.
但我希望保罗·克里格的语音留言正在等我。

489
00:15:02.320 --> 00:15:03.700
Please enter your password.
请输入您的密码。

490
00:15:06.590 --> 00:15:08.690
Oh, and this is when you cover the phone with your hand.
哦，这就是你用手捂住电话的时候。

491
00:15:08.790 --> 00:15:09.570
It's so great.
这太棒了。

492
00:15:09.690 --> 00:15:11.350
You have one new message.
您有一条新留言。

493
00:15:11.350 --> 00:15:13.590
No, no, no, no, no.
不，不，不，不，不。

494
00:15:13.770 --> 00:15:17.310
That is sensitive information only for employees, not outsiders.
这是仅限员工的敏感信息，外人不能看。

495
00:15:17.590 --> 00:15:18.150
Dwight, cut it out.
德怀特，别闹了。

496
00:15:18.210 --> 00:15:18.850
I'm trying to work.
我在工作呢。

497
00:15:19.050 --> 00:15:19.970
You don't work here.
你又不在这工作。

498
00:15:20.030 --> 00:15:20.790
You're not Jim.
你不是吉姆。

499
00:15:21.050 --> 00:15:23.050
Jim, I got us that dinner reservation.
吉姆，我订好晚餐的位子了。

500
00:15:23.270 --> 00:15:23.910
Greek goes 730.
希腊餐厅，7点半。

501
00:15:24.050 --> 00:15:24.470
Oh, great.
哦，太棒了。

502
00:15:24.570 --> 00:15:24.950
Can't wait.
等不及了。

503
00:15:28.780 --> 00:15:32.620
Jim's at the dentist this morning, and Steve is an actor friend of ours.
吉姆今天早上去看牙医了，史蒂夫是我们的一位演员朋友。

504
00:15:32.780 --> 00:15:36.020
I don't know who you are, but you are not Jim.
我不知道你是谁，但你绝对不是吉姆。

505
00:15:36.780 --> 00:15:38.220
This is Jim.
这就是吉姆。

506
00:15:38.800 --> 00:15:40.760
And it's you in the picture frame.
相框里的人也是你。

507
00:15:41.140 --> 00:15:41.680
Yeah.
是啊。

508
00:15:45.260 --> 00:15:47.120
Oh, how did...
哦，怎么会……

509
00:15:48.240 --> 00:15:50.080
And then Dwight's mind melts.
然后德怀特的脑子就当机了。

510
00:15:50.520 --> 00:15:50.920
Yes.
没错。

511
00:15:51.400 --> 00:15:51.820
Yes.
对的。

512
00:15:52.120 --> 00:15:54.680
So that was my entire office experience.
这就是我全部的办公室经历。

513
00:15:55.620 --> 00:15:58.200
And for a cold open, Randall, you had a lot of dialogue.
而且作为一个开场戏，兰德尔，你的台词可真不少。

514
00:15:58.520 --> 00:15:59.040
Yeah, yeah.
对，对。

515
00:15:59.260 --> 00:16:01.160
You had to just rifle it right off.
你得连珠炮似的一气呵成。

516
00:16:01.300 --> 00:16:04.720
Like, it was like you had, you know, been working there the whole time.
感觉就像你，你知道的，已经在那里工作了很久一样。

517
00:16:04.720 --> 00:16:05.360
Yeah, yeah.
是啊，是啊。

518
00:16:05.360 --> 00:16:08.360
It was kind of like medical drama kind of jargon.
有点像医疗剧里的那种专业术语。

519
00:16:08.560 --> 00:16:08.820
There was a lot.
真的有很多。

520
00:16:08.820 --> 00:16:12.020
Like people's names and all the sales and all that.
比如人名、各种销售业绩之类的。

521
00:16:12.040 --> 00:16:12.720
Yeah, yeah.
对，对。

522
00:16:12.800 --> 00:16:13.480
It was a lot.
确实挺多的。

523
00:16:13.660 --> 00:16:16.240
But I, you know, at that point, I was well prepared.
不过我，你知道的，到那个时候已经准备得很充分了。

524
00:16:16.240 --> 00:16:19.960
I think I had some time before the shoot day with the material.
我想在拍摄日前我有一段时间来熟悉这些内容。

525
00:16:20.000 --> 00:16:25.620
And yeah, it was so fun and so surreal just to be acting with you guys on the show that
而且，能和你们这些我深爱的、并且差一点就能加入的剧组合演，真的既有趣又超现实。

526
00:16:25.620 --> 00:16:29.400
I had loved so much and that I got really close to getting, you know.
我曾经跟这个角色擦肩而过。

527
00:16:29.740 --> 00:16:33.080
Well, the writers have shared with us when people would come in that they loved.
编剧们曾跟我们分享过，当他们遇到非常喜欢的试镜演员时——

528
00:16:33.080 --> 00:16:36.960
And for whatever reason, you know, they made the character something different.
不管出于什么原因，他们把角色设定改成了别的样子——

529
00:16:37.440 --> 00:16:41.240
They would have a little folder where they were like people we really liked.
他们会专门建一个文件夹，把我们真正喜欢的演员放进去。

530
00:16:41.440 --> 00:16:43.620
That's why they just called you up and said, come do it.
这就是为什么他们会直接打电话给你，让你来演。

531
00:16:43.680 --> 00:16:44.100
Yeah, yeah.
对，对。

532
00:16:44.400 --> 00:16:48.760
Because they had already fallen in love with you as an actor and thought you were in the
因为他们作为演员已经深深爱上了你，觉得你本来就属于这个剧的世界。

533
00:16:48.760 --> 00:16:49.480
world of the show.
属于这个剧的世界。

534
00:16:49.680 --> 00:16:49.980
Yeah.
对。

535
00:16:49.980 --> 00:16:53.040
I love that that was able to at least come back around in some form.
我很庆幸这件事最终能以某种形式圆满。

