00:19:57.940 --> 00:19:58.420
Amazing.
太棒了。

640
00:19:59.140 --> 00:19:59.620
Amazing.
太棒了。

641
00:19:59.780 --> 00:20:02.160
Do you get recognized from being on The Office?
你因为出演《办公室》而被认出来过吗？

642
00:20:02.880 --> 00:20:04.380
How has that plagued you?
这给你带来了怎样的困扰？

643
00:20:05.080 --> 00:20:08.380
I mean, because people shout random things at us.
我是说，因为人们会向我们大喊各种随机的话。

644
00:20:08.580 --> 00:20:11.440
Someone has shouted to me, green is whore-ish.
有人对我喊过，绿色太荡妇了。

645
00:20:11.880 --> 00:20:14.120
I had on a green, like, tank top.
我当时穿着一件绿色的背心之类的衣服。

646
00:20:14.140 --> 00:20:14.960
And I was like, what?
然后我说，什么？

647
00:20:15.200 --> 00:20:16.180
And then I'm like, oh, right.
接着我想，哦，对了。

648
00:20:17.220 --> 00:20:26.200
Yeah, well, you know, I mean, it was after I filmed it and even after it aired, I didn't get recognized too much from it.
对，好吧，你知道的，我是说，在我拍完之后，甚至在它播出之后，我并没有因此被认出太多。

649
00:20:26.200 --> 00:20:36.620
But eventually, I would say several years later is when it became like a meme and when it started really circulating online.
但最终，我想说在好几年后，它变成了一个梗，并开始在网上广泛流传。

650
00:20:36.900 --> 00:20:44.760
And that's when, yeah, people would, I think I was talking about it on Conan once where, you know, I had kind of forgotten about it.
也就是在那时，对，人们会，我想我以前在柯南的节目里聊过这个，你知道的，我当时差不多都快把它忘了。

651
00:20:44.760 --> 00:20:47.620
Not forgotten about it, but it just wasn't top of mind.
倒不是忘了，只是没一直挂在心上。

652
00:20:47.880 --> 00:20:49.200
Sure, it was a long time ago.
当然，那已经是好久以前的事了。

653
00:20:49.360 --> 00:20:52.060
And somebody screamed out, hey, Asian Jim!
然后有人大喊，嘿，亚裔吉姆！

654
00:20:52.080 --> 00:20:55.760
And I, like, turned around and I thought it was, like, some, like, racial thing.
然后我转过身去，以为是什么种族歧视的事。

655
00:20:57.680 --> 00:21:00.780
Or I didn't know, you know, because I just didn't put it together.
或者我不知道，你知道的，因为我当时没把这联系起来。

656
00:21:01.020 --> 00:21:06.240
And then soon enough, yeah, I'd hear more Asian Jims and I'd go, okay, okay, it's online.
不久之后，没错，我听到更多人叫我亚裔吉姆，我就想，好吧，好吧，这成了网络梗了。

657
00:21:06.520 --> 00:21:06.760
Yeah.
对。

658
00:21:07.100 --> 00:21:07.680
It's online.
在网上火了。

659
00:21:07.680 --> 00:21:16.840
And now, also, in some small way, you guys brought it back because you did this thing with John Krasinski for the trailer for his movie, right?
而且现在，在某种程度上，你们又把这个梗带回来了，因为你们为约翰·卡拉辛斯基的电影预告片做了一场恶搞，对吧？

660
00:21:17.020 --> 00:21:17.880
Yes, for If.
是的，为了《神秘友友》。

661
00:21:17.920 --> 00:21:19.520
That was so funny.
太搞笑了。

662
00:21:19.820 --> 00:21:21.380
How did you even do it?
你们到底是怎么做到的？

663
00:21:21.560 --> 00:21:23.500
You're, like, pranking Ryan Reynolds.
你就像是在捉弄瑞安·雷诺兹。

664
00:21:23.500 --> 00:21:25.860
Because you're saying you are John Krasinski.
因为你宣称自己是约翰·卡拉辛斯基。

665
00:21:25.920 --> 00:21:27.480
And it kind of broke the internet.
这简直有点引爆网络了。

666
00:21:27.760 --> 00:21:29.360
People, like, went berserk for it.
大家简直为之疯狂。

667
00:21:29.360 --> 00:21:33.660
I mean, I think it was such a big thing online for so many years.
我的意思是，我觉得这个梗在网上火了这么多年。

668
00:21:33.660 --> 00:21:38.580
And John was, you know, directing that movie and I don't know if it was Ryan or John.
约翰当时在执导那部电影，我不知道是瑞安还是约翰想出来的。

669
00:21:38.760 --> 00:21:44.140
I think it might have been Ryan who thought, who came up with it and asked if I'd be down to do it.
我觉得可能是瑞安想出来的，他提出了这个创意，并问我愿不愿意参与。

670
00:21:44.260 --> 00:21:45.080
I'm like, yeah, of course.
我说，好啊，当然。

671
00:21:45.320 --> 00:21:45.800
Of course.
当然。

672
00:21:45.960 --> 00:21:46.080
Yeah.
对。

673
00:21:46.340 --> 00:21:53.360
But you had to change your clothes, like, multiple times to be inserted into, like, scenes of you directing the movie.
但你得换好几次衣服，好把自己塞进你执导电影的片场花絮画面里。

674
00:21:53.820 --> 00:21:54.220
Yes.
是的。

675
00:21:54.400 --> 00:21:55.320
Yeah, that's right.
对，没错。

676
00:21:55.480 --> 00:21:55.920
That's right.
没错。

677
00:21:55.960 --> 00:21:56.500
It's really impressive.
这真的很厉害。

678
00:21:56.500 --> 00:21:59.120
I just shot on a green screen in different outfits.
我只是穿着不同的衣服在绿幕前拍摄。

679
00:21:59.120 --> 00:22:06.940
And then they just kind of somehow put me in there, in these shots, BTS shots that they had made for the movie.
然后他们不知怎么就把我塞进去了，塞进了他们为电影拍摄的幕后花絮镜头里。

680
00:22:07.040 --> 00:22:07.620
It was crazy.
太疯狂了。

681
00:22:07.900 --> 00:22:08.640
It was fun.
很有意思。

682
00:22:08.800 --> 00:22:09.540
It was very fun.
非常有意思。

683
00:22:09.700 --> 00:22:12.080
But, yeah, I mean, it just speaks to the power of the internet.
不过，真的，这恰恰说明了互联网的威力。

684
00:22:12.080 --> 00:22:14.180
It was just such a big thing.
它曾经是那么火的一个梗。

685
00:22:14.460 --> 00:22:14.760
Yeah.
对。

686
00:22:15.020 --> 00:22:15.360
Yeah.
对。

687
00:22:15.700 --> 00:22:15.980
Yeah.
对。

688
00:22:16.140 --> 00:22:26.040
And to this day, people are like, it's funny because it was such a big thing online that some people come up to me thinking that I was a regular on the show, you know,
直到今天，人们还觉得，这很有趣，因为这个梗在网上太火了，以至于有些人走过来以为我是剧里的常驻演员，你知道的，

689
00:22:26.120 --> 00:22:27.040
even though I wasn't.
尽管我并不是。

690
00:22:27.200 --> 00:22:28.580
You know, it was just one scene.
你知道，那只是一场戏。

691
00:22:29.280 --> 00:22:31.180
But you stole the scene, you know?
但你抢了风头，不是吗？

692
00:22:31.360 --> 00:22:35.680
I mean, that's all you can ever hope for, no matter, like, how big or small your role.
我的意思是，无论你的角色有多大或多小，这都是你所能期望的全部了。

693
00:22:35.840 --> 00:22:39.340
Like, if you get that moment where you're like, I just owned that.
比如，如果你遇到了那个时刻，你会觉得，我把这场戏彻底拿捏了。

694
00:22:39.620 --> 00:22:39.780
Yeah.
对。

695
00:22:39.840 --> 00:22:44.140
I mean, for me, literally on the day, it was just like, I'm just so happy to be a part of this.
我的意思是，对我来说，在拍摄当天，我真的只是觉得，能参与其中我太高兴了。

696
00:22:44.260 --> 00:22:47.640
I'm just so happy to be on set, on this set in particular.
我只是太高兴能来到片场，尤其是来到这个片场。

697
00:22:47.660 --> 00:22:50.120
And it was one of those, like, okay, that was great.
当时的感觉就是，好吧，这太棒了。

698
00:22:50.500 --> 00:22:51.300
